  "summary": "In the 2x2 factorial control (Prompt Format x Retrieval, N=93), the prompt format effect is substantially larger than the retrieval effect on ROUGE-L and BERTScore. Switching from baseline format to gate-v2 format changed ROUGE-L F1 by +0.0851 (zero-shot) and +0.0727 (RAG), driven by a dramatic increase in precision as output length decreased from ~215.5 words to ~32.9 words. In contrast, the RAG retrieval effect within fixed formats was +0.0143 (baseline format) and +0.0019 (gate-v2 format). For BERTScore F1, the format effect was +0.0700 (zero-shot) and +0.0566 (RAG) vs retrieval effect of +0.0069 (baseline format) and -0.0064 (gate-v2 format). Conclusion: the ROUGE-L improvement previously observed when moving from baseline RAG to relevance_gate_v2 RAG is primarily an output-format/conciseness effect rather than a retrieval precedent effect."
